  "usage": [
    "A very common Cantonese farewell meaning 'goodbye'",
    "Literally means 'see you again', so it can imply meeting again later",
    "Used in both formal and casual situations",
    "Often followed by particles like 喇 for a softer, more natural tone (再見喇)",
    "Can be combined with time words like 聽日再見 (see you tomorrow)"
  ],
